From f1d7045f37bd9093f56d4a1df340e81bd629f58e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:58:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/32] Xbox prelude (engine WCHAR = native wchar_t),
 RegistryClass on a settings file, threads/system shims, and strictness fixes
 found by real Clang

- xbox/include/xbox_prelude.h: force-included; nxdk keeps its WCHAR under another name
- ini/bitstream: WCHAR instead of hard-coded unsigned short; network strings stay 16-bit
- registry_xbox.cpp + xbox_settings_store: RegistryClass backed by a crash-safe file
- _beginthread, GetComputerName/GetUserName, FormatMessage, getpid shims
- thread.cpp: never kill threads on Xbox; wait for cooperative exit
- data.cpp: no Windows string resources on Xbox
- this->, extra qualifications, ctype include, writable buffer in translatedb
